  "findings": [
    "Accuracy and AUC are different measurements. The retained M5 F side arithmetic is reproduced exactly: 865/1689 correct, accuracy0.512137, balanced accuracy0.503929, AUC0.507776; always-UP side accuracy0.519242. No arithmetic error is found on these controlled rows.",
    "M5 October INITIAL to FINAL AUC rises0.534610 to0.565820 while accuracy falls0.551387 to0.539967. Thus a ranking improvement can be hidden by the fixed decision threshold. Its paired training-gain intervals include zero; the FINAL October AUC level itself exceeds0.5 in both pointwise intervals.",
    "Full three-class M5 argmax predicts FLAT on all4096rows and obtains accuracy0.587646, exactly the always-FLAT reference; balanced accuracy is1/3. This is not learned directional selection or Entry coverage.",
    "FINAL October H1 AUC0.647872 exceeds0.5 in both intervals but its FINAL-minus-INITIAL gain is uncertain. M15 October gain+0.107965 excludes0 in both; its absolute FINAL week interval includes0.5. Preserve the distinction between level and training gain.",
    "FINAL December-minus-October H1 AUC -0.202292 excludes0 in both intervals. M5 November/December declines are not robust under both groupings. M15 relative training-change contrasts against October are negative in both intervals for November and December.",
    "Brier probability error increases after training in November M5/M15/H1 and December M5/M15/H1/H4, with both paired intervals positive. H1 December FINAL meanPUP0.809992 contrasts with known-side UP fraction0.398039. This is measured probability miscalibration on that subset, not realized trade loss.",
    "M15 November Brier rises0.059128 while squared mean error falls0.003224 and the residual increases0.062352. A single mean-bias account is insufficient. December squared mean error explains a large algebraic part of several deteriorations, but is not a demonstrated repair or causal attribution.",
    "H4 is a counterexample to a universal October advantage (FINAL November AUC0.629468, uncertain versus0.5). D1 has only4-5 contributing weeks/month, including335 known sides across11days/4weeks in December, and wide intervals. No month/timeframe selection or independent edge claim follows."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Both endpoints share original parents/clocks/nativeFtargets/masks. INITIAL inherits older backbone training and is not a fresh untrained model.",
    "October is first chronological later month, not a selected winning checkpoint/month. All three months and all fiveTF are retained.",
    "The same global UTC-day or Monday-week resampling weights are used in both phases and all months. Month-level intervals have few contributing weeks; zero-support or absent-class draws stay undefined and are counted.",
    "All intervals are pointwise and unadjusted for multiplicity on reused development data. They do not establish independent generalization, stable regime causality or economic edge.",
    "Squared mean error and residual variance sum to Brier. This is descriptive endpoint accounting, not causal attribution, fitted calibration, or feasible shifted probability forecasts.",
    "No new threshold, fit, feature, target, checkpoint or native model action. COT2024 publication/vintage remains UNKNOWN."
  ],
